# =====================================================================================
# semiring.ttl — the SEMIRING rung END-TO-END, the BASE of the two-operation D24 line
# (W2 · SP0 · Stage 3a, T-SEMIRING). Folds FROM fnd:Semiring (basicttl/foundation/algebra_rings.ttl:482+).
# =====================================================================================
# The fully-worked stratified TWO-OPERATION semiring rung, replicating the signed-off ring exemplar
# (spine/ring.ttl) for the BASE rung of the two-operation line. It realises the D24 A0 stratification
# (Syntax ⊥ Theory ⊥ Model ⊥ Element ⊥ ProofArtifact) for a structure with TWO binary operations (+ and ·)
# on ONE carrier, in the D26 full-ladder grammar: a theory record (S,Omega,E) naming sigTwoBinary and the
# SEVEN-law equation set, the B4 TWO model planes (a denotatum + a declaration-record model class linked by
# @rel:denotes), the seven semiring axiom records (each verbatim-derived from the fnd: law + the one-op
# skeleton), the semiring's CHARACTERISTIC two-operation law distributivity decomposed into TWO equation
# records (left x·(y+z)=x·y+x·z, right (y+z)·x=y·x+z·x — the two-sided split, design §1.6), a theorem
# (distributive expansion) + certificate, the triad-envelope gate, and the provenance quartet on records only.
#
# THE SEMIRING = TWO REDUCTS (D24 A6, the base case of ring-as-reducts). A semiring is, by A6, the additive
# COMMUTATIVE-MONOID reduct PLUS the multiplicative-MONOID reduct PLUS distributivity (the interaction law
# gluing them). It is the base rung of the two-operation line — Ring MINUS additive-inverse: its additive
# part is a commutative_monoid (NOT an abelian_group), its multiplicative part a monoid, and distributivity
# is its SOLE added law over the agnostic progenitor (fnd:addsLaw fnd:lawDistributivity, algebra_rings.ttl:513).
# Those reduct EDGES — semiring model-record -> the existing commutative_monoid model-record (the + structure)
# and semiring model-record -> the existing monoid model-record (the · structure), with distributivity as the
# connecting morphism — are minted in reducts_twoop_semiring.ttl (a NEW file, avoiding a write race on the
# committed reducts.ttl and on T-RING's reducts_twoop.ttl). This file mints the semiring theory/denotatum/
# model-record/axioms/equations/theorem/certificate/gate + provenance; the finite semiring witness tables
# are fixtures/semiring_pos.ttl (D24 four-planes: named witnesses are EVIDENCE, outside the ontology data
# glob) with the matching distributivity-violating negative fixtures/semiring_neg.ttl.
#
# WHY THE SATURATING SEMIRING B(2). The witness is the finite saturating semiring on {0,1,2} — additive
# table +sat(a,b)=min(a+b,2), multiplicative table ·sat(a,b)=min(a·b,2). It is a GENUINE semiring that is
# NOT a ring: (S,+,0) is a commutative monoid (associative, commutative, two-sided zero 0), (S,·,1) a
# monoid, · distributes over + on both sides, yet 2 has NO additive inverse (nothing +2 = 0), so the
# additive monoid is NOT a group — the honest semiring-not-ring witness (contrast fnd:ringModel GF(3), a
# field). Its ADDITION is NON-IDEMPOTENT (1+1 = 2, a fresh value), which is exactly what lets the single-cell
# distributivity perturbation of fixtures/semiring_neg.ttl bite cleanly (the Boolean semiring's idempotent
# OR resists single-cell injection). finite:checked and keeps the distributivity tooth
# (shapes/semiring.shapes.ttl SemiringDistributivityShape) non-vacuous and provably biting.
#
# ISOLATION (the two-table / one-op-teeth separation). The one-operation per-law teeth
# (shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl SemigroupAssociativityShape / the commutativity teeth / ModelShape identity ...)
# walk `?cell @rel:structure <model>` with NO operation discriminator; a semiring's MERGED +/· rows scoped
# @rel:structure -> the model would let those teeth mix additive and multiplicative rows and falsely redden.
# So the folded two-operation rows are scoped @rel:structure -> a per-model REIFIED-TABLE node (linked from
# the model by @rel:reified:table), keeping the discriminated two-operation rows OUT of the one-operation
# teeth's `@rel:structure = model` scan — the SAME T4/T5 isolation fnd achieved via the distinct
# fnd:ringStructure predicate (algebra_rings.ttl:79), here achieved via a distinct structure NODE.
# SemiringDistributivityShape walks model -> reified-table -> rows, selecting the additive and multiplicative
# rows by @rel:operation:discriminator (records_twoop.ttl).
#
# HONESTY (Praeriehund; algebra_rings.ttl:30-39). EVERYTHING folded here is SYN: the two-operation line is
# FULLY ABSENT from Helios as algebra (02_algebra_tower.md:134-136; 'semiring' appears only as a valuation-
# coefficient device in optimization, algebra_rings.ttl:487-491, never as an axiomatized rung with +/·
# distributivity axioms), authored as CITED STANDARD SEMIRING/UNIVERSAL ALGEBRA (the Directive 19/20
# precedent: mathematics is fact and liftable, cite the source, never pretend a Helios lift). So
# @rel:authority "SYN" on every RECORD, @rel:proof:status "literature:backed" on the theory (the UNIVERSAL
# semiring theory is cited standard mathematics, NOT finite:checked-from-engine; only the finite B(2) WITNESS
# in fixtures/ carries finite:checked). The theorem is the FOIL distributive expansion (a+b)·(c+d) =
# a·c+a·d+b·c+b·d, honestly derivable from distributivity + additive associativity/commutativity ALONE — it
# does NOT need additive inverse, so unlike a ring's zero-absorption it is a genuine SEMIRING theorem. Every
# [S] token (no runtime precedent) is flagged in an rdfs:comment for the §7.2 maintainer sign-off packet.
#
# NAMING (D26 LOCKED). Full mathematics 12-marker ladder under HEAD (alg:), subdomain 'semiring'. [S] tokens
# flagged. B1 n/a (semiring is not a compound token). B4 two-planes (denotatum kingdom:type…component:type +
# model-record kingdom:class…:model…component:class). B3(a) additive Stage-3a (fnd:Semiring stays byte-intact;
# T-RETIRE is Stage 3c) — skos:exactMatch fnd:Semiring on the denotatum + @rel:historical:identity fnd:Semiring
# on the theory. NOTE: subdomain 'semiring' is ALSO the home of the SHARED two-operation infra (sigTwoBinary,
# the additive/multiplicative operation symbols + discriminators, signatures_twoop.ttl/operations_twoop.ttl/
# records_twoop.ttl), because the two-operation line first enters at this rung; those shared atoms are REUSED
# by IRI, never re-minted here.
#
# Design: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-w2-sp0-primordial-fold-design.md (§1.5, §2, §6 fan-out).
# Folds FROM: basicttl/foundation/algebra_rings.ttl:240-262,284-312,325-333,482-503,652-660.
# ADDITIVE — no fnd:/foundation/* edit (demolition is Stage 3c). Consumes (do not rewrite):
# records.ttl (rec:* classes), records_twoop.ttl (rec:application:two:operation:record + discriminators),
# signatures_twoop.ttl (sigTwoBinary), operations_twoop.ttl (+ · 0 1), spine/monoid.ttl + spine/
# commutative_monoid.ttl (the reduct model-record targets, via reducts_twoop_semiring.ttl). Tooth:
# shapes/semiring.shapes.ttl SemiringDistributivityShape + probes/semiring_law.rq; fixtures/semiring_pos.ttl
# + fixtures/semiring_neg.ttl. Consumed BY: spine/ring.ttl (the ring theory's @rel:reduct -> this semiring
# theory, and the ring model-record owl:disjointWith -> this semiring model-record class, both dangling
# references in ring.ttl until this file lands).

@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix fnd:  <urn:silmaril:fnd:#> .
# mathematics 12-marker ladder head (D26), ending at subdomain::
@prefix alg:  <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:domain:mathematics:realm:algebra:subdomain:> .
# consolidated relation namespace (@rel = @P:relation; records.ttl:41):
@prefix rel:  <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:> .
# plane-type namespace (@typ = @P:type; design §2):
@prefix typ:  <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:type:> .
# reified distributivity term atoms (objects only; no runtime ladder committed for finite worked terms):
@prefix term: <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:term:semiring:> .
# seed-carrier record-class ladder (records.ttl:38-39) — rec:* REUSED:
@prefix rec:  <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:grounding:ontology:basic:formal:domain:knowledge:representation:kingdom:specification:phylum:formal:contract:class:class:order:declared:family:seed:genus:registry:species:> .

# =====================================================================================
# (a) THEORY record — the presented Lawvere theory T=(S,Omega,E) (D24 A6). [S] class:theory/genus:presented
#     Also the Plane-1 DeclarationRecord of the triad envelope (@typ:declaration, design §2g).
#     E = the SEVEN semiring laws (closure / add-assoc / add-comm / add-identity / mult-assoc /
#     mult-identity / distributivity), each an axiom record below, verbatim-derived from the fnd: law.
#     NO additive-inverse — that is the law RING adds over a semiring (spine/ring.ttl). Base two-op rung:
#     like magma (the base one-op rung, spine/magma.ttl:86) it declares NO @rel:reduct (there is no
#     two-operation rung below it); its structural reducts to commutative_monoid + monoid are the
#     ring-as-reducts edges in reducts_twoop_semiring.ttl.
# =====================================================================================
alg:semiring:kingdom:definition:phylum:algebra:class:theory:order:declarative:family:semiring:genus:presented:species:semiring:component:definition:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:theory:record , typ:declaration ;
    rdfs:label "semiring theory (S,Omega,E)" ;
    rel:notation   "semiring" ;
    rel:identifier "urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:domain:mathematics:realm:algebra:subdomain:semiring:kingdom:definition:phylum:algebra:class:theory:order:declarative:family:semiring:genus:presented:species:semiring:component:definition:instance:canonical" ;
    rel:signature  alg:semiring:kingdom:definition:phylum:specification:class:signature:order:two:binary:family:operation:genus:algebraic:species:signature:component:definition:instance:canonical ;
    rel:equation   alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:closure:order:two:binary:family:semiring:genus:product:species:membership:component:statement:instance:canonical ,
                   alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:associativity:order:binary:family:semiring:genus:additive:species:equality:component:statement:instance:canonical ,
                   alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:commutativity:order:binary:family:semiring:genus:additive:species:equality:component:statement:instance:canonical ,
                   alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:identity:order:binary:family:semiring:genus:additive:species:member:component:statement:instance:canonical ,
                   alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:associativity:order:binary:family:semiring:genus:multiplicative:species:equality:component:statement:instance:canonical ,
                   alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:identity:order:binary:family:semiring:genus:multiplicative:species:member:component:statement:instance:canonical ,
                   alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:distributivity:order:two:binary:family:semiring:genus:interaction:species:distribution:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:denotatum  alg:semiring:kingdom:type:phylum:algebra:class:semiring:order:two:binary:family:operation:genus:axiomatic:species:semiring:component:type:instance:canonical ;
    rel:assignment alg:semiring:kingdom:assignment:phylum:reconciliation:class:gate:order:declarative:family:semiring:genus:reconciled:species:declaration:component:assignment:instance:canonical ;
    rel:validation:mode "finite:table" ;
    rel:proof:status    "literature:backed" ;
    rel:created  "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:modified "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:version  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:state    "accepted" ;
    rel:authority "SYN" ;
    rel:historical:identity fnd:Semiring ;
    skos:closeMatch fnd:Semiring ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The presented semiring THEORY record T=(S,Omega,E) (D24 A0 Theory plane, A6), folding fnd:Semiring (algebra_rings.ttl:482-503). S,Omega = @rel:signature sigTwoBinary (signatures_twoop.ttl, Sigma={+,·,0,1}, one carrier sort S, two binary operations, two nullary units — SHARED with ring and field, algebra_rings.ttl:328); E = @rel:equation the SEVEN semiring laws — two-op closure, additive associativity, additive commutativity, additive identity, multiplicative associativity, multiplicative identity and distributivity — each an axiom record below verbatim-derived from the fnd: law (algebra_rings.ttl:240-250,284-312) plus the one-operation skeleton (spine/monoid.ttl, spine/commutative_monoid.ttl). Semiring is Ring MINUS additive-inverse: its additive part is a COMMUTATIVE MONOID (S,+,0) — NOT an abelian group — and its multiplicative part a MONOID (S,·,1); it does NOT carry the additive-inverse law (that is the single law RING adds over a semiring, fnd:Ring fnd:addsLaw fnd:lawAdditiveInverse, algebra_rings.ttl:513, spine/ring.ttl). The semiring's CHARACTERISTIC two-operation law is DISTRIBUTIVITY (· distributes over +), which is ALSO its SOLE added law over the agnostic progenitor (fnd:Semiring fnd:addsLaw fnd:lawDistributivity, algebra_rings.ttl:513) — the interaction that glues the additive and multiplicative structures; it is decomposed into the TWO equation records distribution-left (x·(y+z)=x·y+x·z) and distribution-right ((y+z)·x=y·x+z·x) below (design §1.6 two-sided-law split), which are ALSO the connecting morphism of the D24 semiring-as-reducts decomposition (reducts_twoop_semiring.ttl). It is simultaneously the Plane-1 DeclarationRecord of the triad envelope (@typ:declaration, design §2g): @rel:denotatum -> the Plane-2 semiring denotatum (the mathematical object), @rel:assignment -> the Plane-3 reconciliation gate. There is deliberately NO @rel:reduct: semiring is the BASE of the two-operation line, so — like fnd:Semiring hanging directly off the agnostic progenitor (algebra_rings.ttl:484) and like the base one-operation rung magma (spine/magma.ttl:86, 'deliberately NO @rel:reduct') — there is no two-operation rung below it to forget a law into; its additive commutative-monoid reduct and multiplicative-monoid reduct are STRUCTURE reducts minted in reducts_twoop_semiring.ttl, not a one-step theory-morphism down the two-op line. D24 first-class metadata: @rel:validation:mode 'finite:table' (semiring models are validated by the finite saturating-semiring B(2) Cayley tables) and @rel:proof:status 'literature:backed' (the UNIVERSAL semiring theory is cited standard universal algebra, NOT finite:checked-from-engine — only the finite B(2) WITNESS in fixtures/ is finite:checked, honest per Praeriehund). Provenance quartet (created/modified/version/state) + @rel:authority 'SYN' live on this RECORD, never on the denotatum (D24). SYN: the two-operation line is FULLY ABSENT from Helios as algebra (algebra_rings.ttl:30-35,487-491), authored as cited standard semiring theory. Historical-identity BRIDGE: @rel:historical:identity fnd:Semiring + skos:closeMatch fnd:Semiring (Stage-3a ADDITIVE — fnd:Semiring stays byte-intact; T-RETIRE stubs it in Stage 3c); the denotatum's skos:exactMatch fnd:Semiring keeps inbound SP1/SP2/SP3 fnd:Semiring references resolvable through the fold. This theory is the RESOLUTION target of spine/ring.ttl's ring theory @rel:reduct edge (the forgetful theory-morphism ring |-> semiring, forgetting additive inverse), a dangling reference in ring.ttl until this file lands. Tooth: TheoryShape (min1/max1 signature + min1 equation + identity-collision) + ProofStatusShape + ValidationModeShape + ProvenanceShape. [S] class:theory / genus:presented UNATTESTED (§7.2 #1 mint-more-than-runtime, PIVOTAL); @rel:validation:mode / @rel:proof:status are D24 vocab; all flagged for the sign-off packet." .

# =====================================================================================
# (b1) DENOTATUM — B4 Plane-2: the mathematical object 'a semiring', NO provenance. skos:exactMatch
#      fnd:Semiring (the retire-map bridge SP1/SP2/SP3 fnd:Semiring references resolve through; BridgeShape focus).
# =====================================================================================
alg:semiring:kingdom:type:phylum:algebra:class:semiring:order:two:binary:family:operation:genus:axiomatic:species:semiring:component:type:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:denotatum:record ;
    rdfs:label "semiring" ;
    rel:notation   "semiring" ;
    rel:identifier "urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:domain:mathematics:realm:algebra:subdomain:semiring:kingdom:type:phylum:algebra:class:semiring:order:two:binary:family:operation:genus:axiomatic:species:semiring:component:type:instance:canonical" ;
    skos:exactMatch fnd:Semiring ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The semiring DENOTATUM (B4 LOCKED Plane-2, §7.2 #10): the mathematical object 'a semiring' itself, carrying its canonical @rel:identifier and @rel:notation ONLY — and, critically, NO provenance (D24: provenance lives on the RECORD that declares it, never on the denoted object; V1DenotatumHygieneShape maxCount-0 tooth). It is pointed to by the theory record's @rel:denotatum and the model-record class's @rel:denotes. This IRI (kingdom:type…component:type) is DISTINCT from the model-record class IRI (kingdom:class…component:class) — the two B4 planes. skos:exactMatch fnd:Semiring is the retire-map alias bridge (design §5.2, BridgeShape focus): it keeps every inbound SP1/SP2/SP3 fnd:Semiring reference resolvable THROUGH the fold while fnd:Semiring stays byte-intact until Stage-3c T-RETIRE — the two-operation analogue of the group denotatum skos:exactMatch fnd:Group (bridges.ttl:81) and the ring denotatum skos:exactMatch fnd:Ring (spine/ring.ttl:126). Typed rec:denotatum:record (records.ttl:95-100, cardinality-1 @rel:identifier), which owl:disjointWith rec:declaration:record — one individual is never both the object and the record that declares it. [S] order:two:binary / genus:axiomatic UNATTESTED design-default tokens (order:two:binary echoes sigTwoBinary's two-binary profile), flagged for §7.2 sign-off." .

# =====================================================================================
# (b2) MODEL-RECORD class — B4 Plane-1: the declaration-record model class (owl:Restriction bundle +
#      provenance + disjointness teeth). [S] class:model/genus:governed/component:class. Its ADDITIVE
#      structure is a COMMUTATIVE MONOID + its MULTIPLICATIVE structure is a monoid (the D24
#      semiring-as-reducts, reducts_twoop_semiring.ttl); the reduct edges are minted there, this class is
#      their subject. It is the RESOLUTION target of spine/ring.ttl's ring model-record owl:disjointWith edge.
# =====================================================================================
alg:semiring:kingdom:class:phylum:algebra:class:model:order:declarative:family:semiring:genus:governed:species:semiring:component:class:instance:canonical
    a owl:Class , rec:model:record , rec:declaration:record ;
    rdfs:label "semiring model class" ;
    rel:notation "semiring model" ;
    rel:denotes alg:semiring:kingdom:type:phylum:algebra:class:semiring:order:two:binary:family:operation:genus:axiomatic:species:semiring:component:type:instance:canonical ;
    rdfs:subClassOf
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; owl:onProperty rel:carrier ] ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; owl:onProperty rel:zero:element ] ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; owl:onProperty rel:one:element ] ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; owl:onProperty rel:additive:operation ] ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; owl:onProperty rel:multiplicative:operation ] ;
    owl:disjointWith alg:ring:kingdom:class:phylum:algebra:class:model:order:declarative:family:ring:genus:governed:species:ring:component:class:instance:canonical ,
                     alg:field:kingdom:class:phylum:algebra:class:model:order:declarative:family:field:genus:governed:species:field:component:class:instance:canonical ;
    rel:created  "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:modified "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:version  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:state    "accepted" ;
    rel:authority "SYN" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The semiring MODEL-RECORD class (B4 LOCKED Plane-1, §7.2 #10, design §2b): the declaration-record that carries the owl:Restriction bundle, the provenance quartet and the disjointness teeth, and @rel:denotes exactly one Plane-2 denotatum. It mints kingdom:class:…:model:…:component:class — DISTINCT from the [S] denotatum atom's kingdom:type:…:component:type IRI. The INTENSIONAL owl:Restriction bundle (the fix for the D23 extensional flaw — basicttl/foundation/*.ttl has ZERO owl:Restriction) makes 'a semiring is a set with exactly one carrier, exactly one additive identity 0, exactly one multiplicative identity 1, exactly one additive operation + and exactly one multiplicative operation ·' a graph fact via five cardinality-1 owl:Restrictions on @rel:carrier / @rel:zero:element / @rel:one:element / @rel:additive:operation / @rel:multiplicative:operation (the two-operation counterpart of the monoid model-record's single identity/operation bundle, spine/monoid.ttl, replicating spine/ring.ttl:135-145). The D24 SEMIRING-AS-REDUCTS decomposition — this semiring model-record's ADDITIVE structure IS a COMMUTATIVE MONOID (the existing commutative_monoid model-record, spine/commutative_monoid.ttl:130) and its MULTIPLICATIVE structure IS a monoid (the existing monoid model-record, spine/monoid.ttl:104), glued by distributivity — is minted as forgetful/structure reduct edges in reducts_twoop_semiring.ttl with this class as their subject (bridge-never-duplicate: the reduct edges live in ONE file, not duplicated here). This is the BASE case of ring-as-reducts and the key SEMIRING-vs-RING distinction: a semiring's additive reduct is a commutative_monoid, a RING's additive reduct is an abelian_group (spine/ring.ttl / reducts_twoop.ttl) — the ring UPGRADES the additive commutative monoid to an abelian group by adding additive inverse. owl:disjointWith the ring and field model-record classes (spine/ring.ttl:135 already declares the symmetric ring owl:disjointWith semiring; field is a forward reference T-FIELD mints — the disjointness triple stands regardless, and DifferentFromWitnessShape reddens any sameAs-collapse) — the D25 homonym/distinction teeth: a semiring is not a ring (no additive inverses) and not a field (no additive/multiplicative inverses / mult-commutativity). Provenance quartet + @rel:authority 'SYN' live here (the RECORD plane), never on the denotatum. It is punned a owl:Class (so a concrete B(2) model can be typed against it) AND a rec:model:record / rec:declaration:record (so ModelShape / ProvenanceShape sh:targetClass count it as a data-graph focus and the 0-focus gate is satisfied) — legal OWL2 metaclass punning, exactly as spine/ring.ttl / spine/monoid.ttl and DISTINCT from the frame.ttl domain-class-punning anti-pattern V1 forbids. On this focus ModelShape's identity sh:sparql and SemiringDistributivityShape are vacuously satisfied (the class declares no @rel:identity:element / @rel:reified:table / reified cells); the finite B(2) witness in fixtures/semiring_pos.ttl is where SemiringDistributivityShape bites (and fixtures/semiring_neg.ttl is where its distributivity-violating negative flips it). [S] class:model / genus:governed / component:class UNATTESTED (§7.2 #1/#10) -> sign-off packet." .

# =====================================================================================
# (c) FOUNDATION AXIOM records — the seven members of E (design §2c — minimal, NO denotatum/gate/
#     provenance, NO certificate; axiom != theorem is structural, rec:axiom:record owl:disjointWith
#     rec:theorem:record, records.ttl:119). Each verbatim-derives its fnd: law (algebra_rings.ttl).
#     Six are BASELINE two-operation laws (the additive commutative monoid + multiplicative monoid that
#     PRESENT the semiring); distributivity is the CHARACTERISTIC two-op interaction AND the sole added law.
#     There is deliberately NO additive-inverse axiom — that is the law RING adds over a semiring.
# =====================================================================================
alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:closure:order:two:binary:family:semiring:genus:product:species:membership:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:axiom:record ;
    rdfs:label "semiring two-operation closure" ;
    rel:notation "for all x,y in S: x+y in S and x·y in S" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The two-operation CLOSURE / totality axiom of the semiring theory (rec:axiom:record), folding fnd:lawTwoOpClosure (algebra_rings.ttl:240-244): both binary operations + and · are total functions S,S -> S, so for all x,y in the carrier S the sum x+y and the product x·y are defined and lie in S. A membership/totality statement, NOT a left=right equation — an axiom record only, NOT a rec:equation:record, carrying NO @rel:left/@rel:right. Minimal per design §2c: no denotatum / gate / provenance, no @rel:certificate (an axiom is asserted, not proved). A member of the semiring theory's equation set E. SYN, cited standard universal algebra." .

alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:associativity:order:binary:family:semiring:genus:additive:species:equality:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:axiom:record ;
    rdfs:label "semiring additive associativity" ;
    rel:notation "(a+b)+c = a+(b+c)" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The ADDITIVE-ASSOCIATIVITY axiom of the semiring theory (rec:axiom:record), folding fnd:lawAddAssoc (algebra_rings.ttl:284-288): the addition + is associative, (a+b)+c = a+(b+c), because a semiring's additive part is a COMMUTATIVE MONOID, which demands associativity. genus:additive keeps it distinct from the multiplicative-associativity axiom (genus:multiplicative) on the same class:associativity — the operation-plane analogue of fnd:additiveOp vs fnd:multiplicativeOp. A BASELINE member of E (the additive commutative-monoid part), NOT the semiring's characteristic added law (that is distributivity as the two-op interaction). Minimal per design §2c: no denotatum / gate / provenance / certificate. SYN, cited standard semiring theory." .

alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:commutativity:order:binary:family:semiring:genus:additive:species:equality:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:axiom:record ;
    rdfs:label "semiring additive commutativity" ;
    rel:notation "a+b = b+a" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The ADDITIVE-COMMUTATIVITY axiom of the semiring theory (rec:axiom:record), folding fnd:lawAddComm (algebra_rings.ttl:290-294): the addition + commutes, a+b = b+a, because a semiring's additive part is a COMMUTATIVE monoid. It is ADDITIVE commutativity ONLY — a semiring's MULTIPLICATIVE operation is NOT required to commute (noncommutative semirings, e.g. matrix semirings, and the corpus semiring coefficients, are legitimate algebra; multiplicative commutativity is added exactly at the FIELD rung, fnd:lawFieldMultComm). genus:additive marks the operation. A BASELINE member of E (the additive commutative-monoid part). Minimal per design §2c: no denotatum / gate / provenance / certificate. SYN, cited standard semiring theory." .

alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:identity:order:binary:family:semiring:genus:additive:species:member:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:axiom:record ;
    rdfs:label "semiring additive identity (two-sided zero)" ;
    rel:notation "exists 0: 0+x = x and x+0 = x" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The two-sided ADDITIVE-IDENTITY axiom of the semiring theory (rec:axiom:record), folding fnd:lawAddIdentity (algebra_rings.ttl:296-300): there exists a two-sided additive identity 0 (the zero element, model-plane @rel:zero:element / fnd:hasZeroElement) with 0+x = x AND x+0 = x for every carrier element x — the neutral of the additive COMMUTATIVE MONOID (a semiring's additive part is a commutative monoid, NOT — as in a ring — an abelian group; there is NO additive-inverse law at this rung). genus:additive marks the operation (distinct from the multiplicative-identity axiom's genus:multiplicative). A BASELINE member of E. Held here as a single parent axiom (two-sidedness noted) rather than decomposed into left/right equation records — only the semiring's CHARACTERISTIC law distributivity is decomposed at this rung (design §1.6). Minimal per design §2c: no denotatum / gate / provenance / certificate. SYN, cited standard semiring theory." .

alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:associativity:order:binary:family:semiring:genus:multiplicative:species:equality:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:axiom:record ;
    rdfs:label "semiring multiplicative associativity" ;
    rel:notation "(a·b)·c = a·(b·c)" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The MULTIPLICATIVE-ASSOCIATIVITY axiom of the semiring theory (rec:axiom:record), folding fnd:lawMultAssoc (algebra_rings.ttl:302-306): the multiplication · is associative, (a·b)·c = a·(b·c), because a semiring's multiplicative part is a MONOID. genus:multiplicative keeps it distinct from the additive-associativity axiom (genus:additive) sharing class:associativity — the operation-plane analogue of fnd:multiplicativeOp vs fnd:additiveOp. A BASELINE member of E (the multiplicative-monoid part). Minimal per design §2c: no denotatum / gate / provenance / certificate. SYN, cited standard semiring theory." .

alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:identity:order:binary:family:semiring:genus:multiplicative:species:member:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:axiom:record ;
    rdfs:label "semiring multiplicative identity (two-sided one)" ;
    rel:notation "exists 1: 1·x = x and x·1 = x" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The two-sided MULTIPLICATIVE-IDENTITY axiom of the semiring theory (rec:axiom:record), folding fnd:lawMultIdentity (algebra_rings.ttl:308-312): there exists a two-sided multiplicative identity 1 (the one element, model-plane @rel:one:element / fnd:hasOneElement) with 1·x = x AND x·1 = x for every carrier element x — the neutral of the multiplicative monoid every semiring carries. genus:multiplicative marks the operation (distinct from the additive-identity axiom's genus:additive). A BASELINE member of E. Held as a single parent axiom (two-sidedness noted), not decomposed (only distributivity is decomposed at the semiring rung, design §1.6). Minimal per design §2c: no denotatum / gate / provenance / certificate. SYN, cited standard semiring theory." .

# --- the CHARACTERISTIC two-operation law: distributivity (its own atom; the interaction that glues
#     the additive and multiplicative structures; the connecting morphism of semiring-as-reducts; and
#     the SOLE law semiring adds over the agnostic progenitor, fnd:Semiring fnd:addsLaw fnd:lawDistributivity). ---
alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:distributivity:order:two:binary:family:semiring:genus:interaction:species:distribution:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:axiom:record ;
    rdfs:label "semiring distributivity (two-sided)" ;
    rel:notation "x·(y+z) = x·y + x·z and (y+z)·x = y·x + z·x" ;
    rel:equation alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:distributivity:order:two:binary:family:semiring:genus:interaction:species:distribution:left:component:statement:instance:canonical ,
                 alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:distributivity:order:two:binary:family:semiring:genus:interaction:species:distribution:right:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The DISTRIBUTIVITY axiom of the semiring theory (rec:axiom:record, the named parent law, no side segment), folding fnd:lawDistributivity (algebra_rings.ttl:246-250): the multiplication · distributes over the addition + on BOTH sides — x·(y+z) = x·y + x·z (left) AND (y+z)·x = y·x + z·x (right). This is the CHARACTERISTIC two-operation law of the semiring AND its SOLE added law over the agnostic progenitor (fnd:Semiring fnd:addsLaw fnd:lawDistributivity, algebra_rings.ttl:513) — the sole law CONNECTING the two operations, the interaction that makes a set with two monoid structures a semiring rather than an unrelated pair (Helios has NO +/× distributivity axioms, algebra_rings.ttl:246-250). As a TWO-SIDED law it @rel:equation-decomposes into the TWO reified equation records distribution-left and distribution-right below (design §1.6, §3; right distributivity does NOT follow from left in a noncommutative semiring, so both sides are members of E). It is the D24 semiring-as-reducts CONNECTING MORPHISM: the additive-commutative-monoid reduct and the multiplicative-monoid reduct are glued by exactly this law (reducts_twoop_semiring.ttl @rel:connects both). It is a member of the semiring theory's equation set E, and its added-law status is teeth-proved CLASS-GENERAL by shapes/semiring.shapes.ttl SemiringDistributivityShape / probes/semiring_law.rq over the finite B(2) reified tables: x·(y+z) != x·y + x·z for some triple -> RED (the probe of record perturbs one multiplicative row so a triple fails). Minimal per design §2c: no denotatum / gate / provenance / certificate. SYN, cited standard semiring theory. [S] class:distributivity / genus:interaction / species:distribution UNATTESTED design-default tokens (§7.2 #5) -> sign-off packet." .

# =====================================================================================
# (d) EQUATION records — the two-sided DISTRIBUTIVITY split (design §2d, §1.6). The semiring's
#     characteristic two-operation law reified as an ordered pair per side. distribution-left
#     (x·(y+z) = x·y+x·z) + distribution-right ((y+z)·x = y·x+z·x). Distinct @rel:left terms so the
#     EquationRecordShape identity-collision sh:sparql never fires between the twins (or against ring's).
# =====================================================================================
alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:distributivity:order:two:binary:family:semiring:genus:interaction:species:distribution:left:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:equation:record ;
    rdfs:label "semiring distributivity (left: x·(y+z) = x·y + x·z)" ;
    rel:notation "x·(y+z) = x·y + x·z" ;
    rel:left  term:distribution:leftproduct ;
    rel:right term:distribution:leftsum ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The LEFT-DISTRIBUTIVITY law x·(y+z) = x·y + x·z — side 1 of the semiring's two-sided distributivity, reified as an equation record (rec:equation:record) with one @rel:left term (the product x·(y+z)) and one @rel:right term (the sum x·y + x·z). A two-sided law mints TWO equation records, one per side (design §1.6, §3). It is the member the distributivity parent axiom @rel:equation-decomposes into and the EquationRecordShape cardinality-1 left/right focus; it is ALSO the arithmetic content the SemiringDistributivityShape sh:sparql checks over the finite B(2) reified tables (form x·(y+z) via an additive then a multiplicative row; form x·y + x·z via two multiplicative rows then an additive row; compare). Its @rel:left/@rel:right terms live in the semiring: term namespace (urn:silmaril:…:relation:term:semiring:), DISTINCT from spine/ring.ttl's ring: term namespace, so the EquationRecordShape identity-collision clause does not fire against the ring distributivity records. SYN, cited standard semiring theory. [S] the species:distribution:left SIDE SEGMENT is UNATTESTED (§7.2 #2 side-segment placement) -> sign-off packet." .

alg:semiring:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:distributivity:order:two:binary:family:semiring:genus:interaction:species:distribution:right:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:equation:record ;
    rdfs:label "semiring distributivity (right: (y+z)·x = y·x + z·x)" ;
    rel:notation "(y+z)·x = y·x + z·x" ;
    rel:left  term:distribution:rightproduct ;
    rel:right term:distribution:rightsum ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The RIGHT-DISTRIBUTIVITY law (y+z)·x = y·x + z·x — side 2 of the semiring's two-sided distributivity, reified as an equation record (rec:equation:record) with one @rel:left term (the product (y+z)·x) and one @rel:right term (the sum y·x + z·x). Its twin is the distribution-LEFT record above; together they are the TWO equation records the ONE two-sided distributivity law decomposes into (design §1.6, §3). Right distributivity does NOT follow from left in a noncommutative semiring, so it is an independent member of E (in the commutative B(2) witness both sides coincide). Distinct @rel:left term (rightproduct) from the left record (leftproduct) and in the semiring: term namespace (distinct from ring's), so the EquationRecordShape identity-collision sh:sparql does not fire between the twins or against the ring records. SYN, cited standard semiring theory. [S] species:distribution:right SIDE SEGMENT UNATTESTED (§7.2 #2) -> sign-off packet." .

# =====================================================================================
# (f) THEOREM + CERTIFICATE (design §2f — a theorem with a digest+proof-method certificate, NEVER an
#     axiom; the closure.ttl Yoneda theorem/certificate idiom). Semiring's natural structure theorem:
#     the DISTRIBUTIVE EXPANSION of a product of sums, (a+b)·(c+d) = a·c + a·d + b·c + b·d — a genuine
#     consequence of distributivity + additive associativity/commutativity, needing NO additive inverse
#     (so it is a true SEMIRING theorem, unlike a ring's zero-absorption which requires additive inverse).
# =====================================================================================
alg:semiring:kingdom:theorem:phylum:algebra:class:expansion:order:declarative:family:semiring:genus:distributive:species:expansion:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:theorem:record ;
    rdfs:label "semiring distributive expansion" ;
    rel:notation "for all a,b,c,d: (a+b)·(c+d) = a·c + a·d + b·c + b·d" ;
    rel:certificate alg:semiring:kingdom:certificate:phylum:algebra:class:expansion:order:declarative:family:semiring:genus:distributive:species:expansion:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:authority "SYN" ;
    rel:created  "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:modified "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:version  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:state    "accepted" ;
    rdfs:comment "Theorem, not an additional foundational axiom (design §2f, the closure.ttl Yoneda theorem/certificate idiom): in any semiring (S,+,·,0,1) a product of two sums EXPANDS as (a+b)·(c+d) = a·c + a·d + b·c + b·d. It is a DERIVED consequence of distributivity (both sides) together with additive associativity and commutativity — (a+b)·(c+d) = (a+b)·c + (a+b)·d by left distributivity = (a·c + b·c) + (a·d + b·d) by right distributivity = a·c + a·d + b·c + b·d by additive assoc/comm — NOT a new axiom (the D24 A0 ProofArtifact plane). CRITICALLY it uses ONLY the seven semiring laws and needs NO additive inverse, so it is a genuine SEMIRING theorem — DISTINCT from a ring's zero-absorption 0·x=0 (spine/ring.ttl), which the semiring rung deliberately does NOT claim because in a general semiring 0·x=0 does NOT follow without additive inverse (and fnd:eqsSemiring does not include an absorbing-zero law, algebra_rings.ttl:346-359). It is the semiring's natural structure theorem the distributivity law licenses. It is a rec:theorem:record carrying a @rel:certificate (a proof artifact with a digest + proof-method), NEVER a rec:axiom:record — the theorem/axiom collapse is forbidden (rec:axiom:record owl:disjointWith rec:theorem:record, records.ttl:119; design §2f). Provenance quartet + @rel:authority 'SYN' on the record (the distributivity law it derives from is SYN, algebra_rings.ttl:246-250)." .

alg:semiring:kingdom:certificate:phylum:algebra:class:expansion:order:declarative:family:semiring:genus:distributive:species:expansion:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , typ:certificate ;
    rdfs:label "semiring distributive expansion certificate" ;
    rel:digest:value    "8530e7f85c8880e8983c49904ec57786139c1f51d5c5c57afb4ff8657baf58ce" ;
    rel:proof:method    "Explicit general mathematical derivation ((a+b)·(c+d) = (a+b)·c + (a+b)·d by left distributivity; = (a·c+b·c)+(a·d+b·d) by right distributivity; = a·c+a·d+b·c+b·d by additive associativity and commutativity; uses only the seven semiring laws, no additive inverse); not proof-assistant checked" ;
    rel:source:location "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-w2-sp0-primordial-fold-design.md#2f" ;
    rdfs:comment "The proof CERTIFICATE for semiring distributive expansion (design §2f; the closure.ttl certificate idiom): a proof artifact carrying @rel:digest:value (the SHA-256 of the canonical proof statement 'Semiring distributive expansion: in any semiring (S,+,.,0,1) for all a,b,c,d in S, (a+b).(c+d) = a.c + a.d + b.c + b.d. Proof: (a+b).(c+d) = (a+b).c + (a+b).d by left distributivity; = (a.c + b.c) + (a.d + b.d) by right distributivity; = a.c + a.d + b.c + b.d by additive associativity and commutativity. Uses only the seven semiring laws (no additive inverse). General mathematical derivation; not proof-assistant checked'), @rel:proof:method (an explicit general derivation, honestly NOT a proof-assistant certificate — D20 honesty) and @rel:source:location. It is typed @typ:certificate, NEVER an axiom — an axiom is asserted, a certificate records a derivation. This is the ProofArtifact plane made concrete: the theorem points at it via @rel:certificate, so a theorem stripped of its certificate is detectable, and an axiom masquerading as a proved theorem is caught by the axiom/theorem disjointness (records.ttl:119)." .

# =====================================================================================
# (g) GATE — the Plane-3 reconciliation gate of the triad envelope (design §2g, @typ:gate).
# =====================================================================================
alg:semiring:kingdom:assignment:phylum:reconciliation:class:gate:order:declarative:family:semiring:genus:reconciled:species:declaration:component:assignment:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , typ:gate ;
    rdfs:label "semiring declaration reconciliation gate" ;
    rel:check:status   "declaration reconciled; not a generic semantic proof" ;
    rel:interpreted:by alg:semiring:kingdom:interpretation:phylum:reconciliation:class:declaration:order:declarative:family:semiring:genus:reconciled:species:semiring:component:interpretation:instance:canonical ;
    rdfs:comment "The Plane-3 reconciliation GATE of the semiring declaration triad envelope (design §2g): the theory record (@typ:declaration) @rel:assignment-points at this gate, which records that the semiring declaration was RECONCILED against its Plane-2 denotatum — @rel:check:status 'declaration reconciled; not a generic semantic proof' (the honest scope: the gate reconciles the declaration to the denoted object, it does not claim a universal semantic proof) — and @rel:interpreted:by an interpretation atom. Typed @typ:gate. This is the per-record triad-envelope gate INSTANCE (Plane-3), NOT a gate SPECIFICATION class (the two-ladder ruling, design §4 / §7.2 #8: gate/clause SPECS mint the core:entity gate ladder; this per-record gate instance rides the mathematics ladder scoped to the semiring rung). It closes the Denotatum/DeclarationRecord/Gate triad (D24 four planes) so the semiring declaration is reconciled, not merely asserted." .
